# AWS EC2 Nginx Web Server Setup

This repository documents the provisioning and deployment of an Nginx web server on AWS EC2 as part of the Nautilus project initial infrastructure setup.

## Task Overview

The goal was to set up a public-facing EC2 instance running Nginx on Ubuntu in the `us-east-1` region using the AWS CLI.

### Specifications Required:
* **Instance Name:** `devops-ec2`
* **AMI:** Ubuntu 22.04 LTS (Jammy Jellyfish)
* **Region:** `us-east-1`
* **Security Group:** Allows inbound HTTP traffic on **Port 80** from `0.0.0.0/0`.
* **User Data:** Automatically installs, enables, and starts Nginx upon launch.

---

## Deployment Steps

### 1. Set Default AWS Region
```bash
aws configure set default.region us-east-1
2. Identify Default VPC & Create Security Group
Bash
# Retrieve the default VPC ID
VPC_ID=$(aws ec2 describe-vpcs --filters "Name=isDefault,Values=true" --query "Vpcs[0].VpcId" --output text)

# Create Security Group for HTTP traffic
SG_ID=$(aws ec2 create-security-group \
  --group-name web-server-sg \
  --description "Allow HTTP traffic" \
  --vpc-id $VPC_ID \
  --query 'GroupId' --output text)

# Authorize inbound HTTP traffic on port 80
aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress \
  --group-id $SG_ID \
  --protocol tcp \
  --port 80 \
  --cidr 0.0.0.0/0
3. Create User Data Script
Bash
cat << 'EOF' > userdata.sh
#!/bin/bash
apt-get update -y
apt-get install -y nginx
systemctl start nginx
systemctl enable nginx
EOF
4. Fetch Ubuntu AMI & Launch EC2 Instance
Bash
# Get latest Ubuntu 22.04 LTS AMI ID
AMI_ID=$(aws ec2 describe-images \
  --owners 099720109477 \
  --filters "Name=name,Values=ubuntu/images/hvm-ssd/ubuntu-jammy-22.04-amd64-server-*" "Name=state,Values=available" \
  --query 'reverse(sort_by(Images, &CreationDate))[0].ImageId' --output text)

# Launch EC2 instance
aws ec2 run-instances \
  --image-id $AMI_ID \
  --instance-type t2.micro \
  --security-group-ids $SG_ID \
  --user-data file://userdata.sh \
  --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=instance,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=devops-ec2}]'
Verification
Check Instance Status and Public IP:

Bash
